    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§89-s, 445, 603, 604 & 605-e, R & SS L",
    "lawSection": "Retirement and Social Security Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S2934\n\nSPONSOR: KAMINSKY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the retirement and social security law, in relation to\nthe retirement of members who serve as police medics, police medic\nsupervisors and members who perform police medic related services in the\nNassau county police department\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis legislation amends state law to reflect recent nomenclature changes\nmade by the Nassau County Civil Service Commission.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends sections 89-s*2, 445, 603, 604, and 605-e of the\nRetirement and Social Security Law that relate to certain Nassau County\nPolice Department employees. To reflect recent title changes made by the\nNassau County Civil Service Commission, this legislation adds the titles\nof police medic, police medic supervisor, and police medic coordinator\nto the list of those eligible for certain retirement benefits.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nIn the spring and summer of 2019, the County of Nassau Civil Service\nCommission approved a change to the existing titles of Ambulance Medical\nTechnician, Ambulance Medical Technician Supervisor, and Ambulance\nMedical Technician Coordinator to Police Medic, Police Medic Supervisor,\nand Police Medic Coordinator, respectively.\n\nThis legislation creates no new benefits. It simply amends several\nsections of state retirement and social security law that use the previ-\nous titles for certain benefits. The employees in these new police medic\ntitles were already entitled to these benefits under the previous\ntitles. This legislation simply ensures that they continue to be eligi-\nble for these benefits while working under their new titles that were\ncreated and approved by the Nassau County Civil Service Commission.\n\nThe previously used titles, Ambulance Medical Technician, Ambulance\nMedical Technician Supervisor, and Ambulance Medical Technician Coordi-\nnator, will remain in statute to ensure that incumbents will receive\nproper service credit for their work in these formerly used titles.\nHowever, the County will not be hiring any new employees into these\ntitles in the future.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2020: S7112, Kaminsky. Passed Senate, Died in Assembly.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNo new costs.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
